# (2026-10-26, "you can ship it"): seat 0 holds two different lands in hand — Forest and
# Mountain, different names so the e2e can tell which one it actually played, same device
# `land-into-middle.state` uses — and nothing else interesting, an uncontested turn-1 Main Phase 1.
# Playing the first succeeds; the second press is refused ("not-offered") with
# NumLandThisTurn (1) == MaxLandPlay (1) — the exact shape the mistake bubble's "land" classifier
# (`apps/ui/src/play/live/mistakes.ts`) answers for certain. Used by
# `e2e/af409-mistake-bubble.spec.ts`.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=Forest;Mountain
humanbattlefield=
humanlibrary=Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest
aigraveyard=
